🔹 Pehle yeh samjho — Route kya hota hai?
📍 Route ka matlab:
Jab koi user browser ya Postman se ek URL pe request bhejta hai, to us URL ko handle karne ke liye hum jo code likhte hain, usse Route kehte hain.

🧠 Example:
js
Copy code
app.get('/hello', (req, res) => {
  res.send('Hello World!');
});
Yeh route GET request ko handle karta hai jo /hello pe aati hai.

/hello = path

app.get(...) = route handler

🔸 Ab Router kya hota hai?
🧳 Router = Ek chhoti Express wali file jo routes ko group karke rakhti hai
Jab tumhare paas bahut saare routes ho jaate hain, to code bada aur messy ho jaata hai. Router ka kaam hai: sab related routes ko alag file me organize karna, taki code clean rahe.

🔧 Router kaise kaam karta hai?
⚙️ 3 Steps me kaam samjho:
🥇 Step 1: Ek router banate hain
js
Copy code
// file: routes/people.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

router.post('/people', (req, res) => {
  const { name } = req.body;
  if (!name) {
    return res.status(400).json({ success: false, msg: 'Naam do bhai!' });
  }
  res.status(201).json({ success: true, person: name });
});

module.exports = router;
🥈 Step 2: Router ko main file me laake use karte hain
js
Copy code
// file: app.js ya index.js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const peopleRouter = require('./routes/people');

app.use(express.json()); // req.body ko read karne ke liye
app.use('/api', peopleRouter); // 👈 Router ko /api path pe mount kiya

app.listen(5000, () => {
  console.log("Server chalu hai port 5000 pe");
});
🥉 Step 3: Ab tum Postman se request bhejo:
bash
Copy code
POST http://localhost:5000/api/people
/api = jahan router mount hai

/people = router me likha hua route

Final path = /api/people

📌 Router vs Route (Difference)
Term	Kya hai	Example
Route	Ek URL path + usko handle karne wala function	/login, /register, etc.
Router	Route ki group file	routes/people.js

🎁 Easy Analogy – "Building Example"
App.js = Main building ka darwaza

Router = Alag-alag departments (jaise: People department)

Route = Har department ke andar table/desk jahan kaam hota hai

So:

/api → People Department

/people → Us department ka ek desk

✅ Summary (Ek Line me):
Route = Ek particular path jahan user request bhejta hai.
Router = Ek file jahan hum multiple related routes rakhte hain.
app.use('/api', router) = Router ko app me connect karna so that route ka path /api/something ban jaye.

Agar chaho to main tumhare liye poori working code structure bana ke de sakta hoon .js files ke saath.

